v 3
d 'DUVM': module to estimate Deaton's unit-value model
d
d  duvm estimates the unit-value model of Deaton (1988, 1990, 1997 ch. 5):
d  own- and cross-price elasticities of quantity, expenditure elasticities
d  and quality elasticities for a group of goods, from the budget shares and
d  the unit values that households report, using the spatial variation of
d  prices across clusters. It follows the book, in closed form and in Mata: a
d  within-cluster first stage, a between-cluster second stage with the
d  errors-in-variables correction, the quality correction through the
d  separability parameter, the completion of the system with a composite good
d  and an approximate Slutsky symmetry. Standard errors are linearized from
d  the influence functions of both stages, by cluster or by survey design
d  (svyset), or come from a design bootstrap of both stages. duvm also
d  corrects the unit values for the selection of the buyers (Heckman, the
d  probit in the standard errors), reports the elasticities of the household,
d  of the individual or of the market, and makes the household size optional.
d  duvmdiag and estat diagnostics check the price signal; predict and estat
d  engel give the Engel curves; tables with significance stars can be written
d  to Word, LaTeX, Excel, CSV or Markdown; a dialog box and help examples run
d  from clickable links are included. Option compat reproduces the Stata code
d  published with Deaton (1997). A technical note documents the model, the
d  estimator and the validation of the variance; it is included as an
d  ancillary file (duvm_technical_note.pdf) and on Zenodo:
d  https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22938872
d
d KW: unit values
d KW: quality
d KW: price elasticities
d KW: demand
d KW: household survey
d KW: survey design
d KW: Deaton
d
d Requires: Stata version 14.2
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261001
d
d Author: Abdelkrim Araar, Universite Laval and Partnership for Economic Policy (PEP)
d Support: email aabd@ecn.ulaval.ca
d
d (A copy of the package as submitted to the SSC archive, version 1.2.1, to
d test it before SSC publishes it: the example data and the other ancillary
d files are copied to the current folder by net get.)
d
f duvm.ado
